    <string name="footer_app_ignored_not_registered">%1$s apps without MiPush SDK</string>
    <string name="status_app_not_registered_detail_without_fake_suggest"><![CDATA[
Registration is determined and initiated by the application and generally begins automatically when the application is launched. Some apps are only registered when finding a XiaoMi devices. See also: <b><a href="https://github.com/MiPushFramework/MiPushFramework/wiki/%E5%BA%94%E7%94%A8%E7%A8%8B%E5%BC%8F%E6%B3%A8%E5%86%8C%E9%97%AE%E9%A2%98%E8%A7%A3%E5%86%B3%E6%96%B9%E6%A1%88">应用程式注册问题解决方案</a></b> and <b><a href="https://github.com/MiPushFramework/MiPushFramework/wiki/%5B%E5%B8%AE%E5%8A%A9%5D-%E5%BA%94%E7%94%A8%E6%B3%A8%E5%86%8C%E9%97%AE%E9%A2%98">[帮助] 应用注册问题</a></b>.
    ]]></string>
    <string name="status_app_not_registered_detail_with_fake_suggest"><![CDATA[
Registration is determined and initiated by the application and generally begins automatically when the application is launched. MiPushFramework will first try its own runtime compatibility and force-register path. If registration has already failed, been reversed, or the local registration state remains inconsistent, try <b><a href="https://github.com/Seyud/device_faker">Device Faker</a></b> in <b>resetprop</b> mode to spoof the target app as a MIUI / Xiaomi device. That mode can modify read-only properties and automatically restore them after the app exits or focus switches. Configuration details: <b><a href="https://github.com/Seyud/device_faker/blob/main/docs/CONFIG.md">CONFIG.md</a></b>. See also: <b><a href="https://github.com/MiPushFramework/MiPushFramework/wiki/%E5%BA%94%E7%94%A8%E7%A8%8B%E5%BC%8F%E6%B3%A8%E5%86%8C%E9%97%AE%E9%A2%98%E8%A7%A3%E5%86%B3%E6%96%B9%E6%A1%88">应用程式注册问题解决方案</a></b> and <b><a href="https://github.com/MiPushFramework/MiPushFramework/wiki/%5B%E5%B8%AE%E5%8A%A9%5D-%E5%BA%94%E7%94%A8%E6%B3%A8%E5%86%8C%E9%97%AE%E9%A2%98">[帮助] 应用注册问题</a></b>.
    ]]></string>
